Package: efaTrail
Type: Package
Title: Sequential Multi-Construct Exploratory Factor Analysis with Audit-Trail Reporting
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Diana", "Rosita", role = c("aut")),
    person("Muhammad", "Sukirlan", email = "muhammad_sukirlan@yahoo.co.id",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Nurlaksana Eko", "Rusminto", role = c("aut")),
    person("Budi", "Kadaryanto", role = c("aut"))
    )
Description: Orchestrates exploratory factor analysis (EFA) across every
    construct (sub-scale) of a multidimensional instrument in sequence,
    iteratively removing items with low factor loadings, strong
    cross-loadings, or high uniqueness, and records every decision at
    every iteration. Unlike existing single-pool item-purification tools
    (e.g. 'ItemRest' on CRAN, or 'efa_utils' on PyPI for Python), which
    purify one item set at a time and leave the researcher to repeat the
    process by hand across sub-scales and write up each step, efaTrail
    automates both the multi-construct orchestration and the generation
    of a publication-ready audit-trail report, of the kind researchers
    have traditionally compiled manually as a supplementary appendix
    during scale development.
